00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:46.720
He Lindsey Graham was subpoenaed in the Georgia
grand jury investigation of Trump's attempt

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:52.210
to overturn to Steele, let's call it what
it is to steal the Georgia electoral votes.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.070
Lindsey Graham, upon receiving the subpoena,
said, I'm going to fight this subpoena.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.719
His lawyers used all sorts of different arguments
and a judge has said, no, you've got to show

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:01.719
up.

00:01:01.719 --> 00:01:03.630
Let's take a look at this NBC News report.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:09.610
A judge ordered Senator Lindsey Graham to
testify in front of a special grand jury in

00:01:09.610 --> 00:01:14.970
Georgia investigating former President Donald
Trump's alleged attempts to overturn the results

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:16.650
of the 2020 election.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:20.970
Fulton County Superior Court Judge Robert
McBurney ordered that Graham will be required

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:22.880
to testify August 2nd.

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.440
The judge's certification, filed Monday, describes
Graham as a necessary and material witness

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.020
to the grand jury probe.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.540
The development was reported earlier by WSB
TV.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:36.310
Graham's office did not immediately respond
to requests for comment.

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:39.810
The senator's attorney said last week he would
not comply.

00:01:39.810 --> 00:01:45.340
The grand jury also subpoenaed members of
Trump's former legal team, including personal

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.280
lawyer Rudy Giuliani.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:53.310
Now, one of the arguments that Lindsey is
lawyers made in this entire thing is that

00:01:53.310 --> 00:02:00.170
his actions in calling Georgia officials to
ask what's going on, can we get the right

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:05.590
count, whatever he was doing, the argument
his lawyers made was that Lindsey's actions

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:11.950
are protected under these constitutional safeguards
for members of Congress not getting punished

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:17.099
for their speech or actions performed in the
course of their legislative duties.

00:02:17.099 --> 00:02:21.450
So to explain that in layman's terms.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.230
The lawyers for Lindsay said.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:29.930
When Lindsay called to inquire about those
election results, he was performing legislative

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.520
duties as a senator of the United States.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:35.739
That probably sounds like B.S. to you.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:36.739
And it is.

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:43.420
And both the D.A. and the judge said Graham
isn't a Georgia resident and Graham is not

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.160
a Georgia politician.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:52.730
And U.S. senators don't have any legitimate
congressional function in personally calling

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:58.010
state election officials to argue about the
results or to suggest that the results might

00:02:58.010 --> 00:02:59.010
be wrong.

00:02:59.010 --> 00:03:00.060
It's it doesn't make any sense.

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:01.060
It's not right.

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:03.480
As a senator, he has no role there.

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.590
He has no standing.

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:05.590
He's not a voter.

00:03:05.590 --> 00:03:07.160
So he can't use that argument.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:11.610
What he was doing was he was trying to trade
on his name and influence by calling and saying,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:12.830
hey, this is Lindsey Graham.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.220
I'm a U.S. senator.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:15.800
I'm paying attention to what you're doing.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:20.090
Don't you think maybe you could review the
results and maybe see if they weren't right?

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:24.239
But there was no legitimate legislative function
as a U.S. senator being served there.

00:03:24.239 --> 00:03:26.520
And unfortunately, the judge agreed with that.

00:03:26.520 --> 00:03:29.420
You don't get to choose which laws you would
like to follow.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.310
I mean, sometimes these people in power do.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.290
But you shouldn't get to anyway.

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:36.470
And Lindsey Graham, at least for now.

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:40.940
And we'll see if he appeals the decision,
if it's subject to appeal or what he tries

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.209
to do between now and August 2nd.

00:03:44.209 --> 00:03:47.349
In principle, he is supposed to show up and
testify on August 2nd.

00:03:47.349 --> 00:03:49.470
I know that clearly his lawyers don't want
him to.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:52.220
That's why they tried every possible argument
to get him out of it.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.260
And if indeed he does testify, it should be
absolutely fascinating.

